  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Dry, tranquil and increasingly milder into the \nweekend \n\nBarely a cloud seen across the entire Mid Atlantic, Central\nAppalachians and Ohio Valley region this midday hour thanks to \na significant and slightly positive tilt Omega Block extending \nfrom Texas to the Upper Great Lakes region with an associated \n1038 mB sfc high centered over West Va this midday hour. \n\nLow pressure will form over the Bahamas late this week and roll\nnorth along the East Coast. There are differences to how each \nmodel and members of the major EFSs track this system. But, they\nall agree we will be in the squeeze between that storm and the \ncold front approaching from the west at the very same time. The \nfront loses almost all of it's moisture and the trough aloft may\narrive quickly enough to push that coastal low and it's precip \noff to the east of PA. But, enough uncertainty exists to keep \nmentioning PoPs and perhaps nudge them up 10% for Sun-Sun PM. \n\nAnother low may form over the Deep South or along the eastern \nshore. That feature has a chance to make precip for the CWA \nsometime between Wed (Day8) and Fri (Day10). Of course, Day 9 is\nThanksgiving. Temp profiles may generate non-liquid precip. So,\nwe'll need to monitor the evolution of this potential system \nvery carefully. \n\nOf course, this dry stretch with plenty of sun is crisping up \nthe fuels for wildfires. RHs dip into the 20s in southern areas\ntoday and almost everywhere Thursday. Thankfully, the wind is \nlight through the rest of the week.",
